		{
			title: "The Price is Light"
			icon: "tfb2:factory_crate_incomplete"
			x: 1.25d
			y: 2.8125d
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "Crystal Costs and You"
			description: [
				"&dInteresting on having to &n&lpay to make Vault Crystals&r&d. You would think they would want you in and out of the Vaults as easily as possible."
				""
				"&5Well, there does seem to be &n&la game setting for making them like that&r&5, but paying for crystals is, how you say, the default mode?"
				""
				"&dWhy...let me look at something here..."
				""
				"&5What did you find, sis?"
				""
				"&dThe Crystals mostly cost... &n&lFactory Crates&r&d, by the look of it. Easy to make. &n&lCraft some Empty Factory Crates, then craft them with the listed items&r&d. But the &n&lmore Crystals you make, the number of crates will grow&r&d. And the more 'difficult' items are required for the crates."
				""
				"&5Hmm, thats interesting. So you'll have to &n&lpay more to be able to go into Vaults&r&5..."
				""
				"&dAnd you'll &n&lwant to go into more Vaults to get more gear and to level up&r&d. And it looks like many of the subsystems you can unlock primarily help you get MORE of the items you need for Crystals."
			]
